Yes, but we were talking about whether this tactic decreases survival on a
per-character basis or not.  Take as another example David's hypothetical
strategy of quaffing from early fountains in the hopes of a wish.  This
will result in more deaths in the early game due to water moccasins etc.,
but occasionally will produce a character with, say, GDSM.  It may be a
valid strategy for you as a player, but it's not the best option for a
particular character.

Please don't think I'm somehow criticizing the protection racket as a bad
strategy, but I suspect David and others are correct in their suspicions
that it is not optimal if your goal is a high ascension/death ratio.  If,
on the other hand, your goal is a high ascenson/playing time ratio, the
story may be different.

